\t  \"Return the deterministic CBOR bytes (byte[] / Uint8Array / Uint8List)\n   281\t   of v -- the exact bytes content hashing digests, so\n   282\t   `(digest-bytes algo (canonical-bytes v))` is\n   283\t   `(content-hash v {:algorithm algo})`.\n   284\t   This is the byte form Jing content travels in across a `dao.stream`\n   285\t   boundary.\"\n   286\t  [v]\n   287\t  (cbor/encode v))\n   288\t\n   289\t\n   290\t(defn content-hash\n   291\t  \"Hash the canonical-bytes of v using the specified algorithm (defaulting to\n   292\t   default-hash-algorithm, i.e. :blake3). Returns lowercase hexadecimal string.\n   293\t   Arities: [v] and [v {:keys [algorithm]}].\"\n   294\t  ([v]\n   295\t   (content-hash v {:algorithm default-hash-algorithm}))\n   296\t  ([v opts]\n   297\t   (let [algo (clojure.core/get opts :algorithm default-hash-algorithm)]\n   474\t(defn materialize!\n   475\t  \"Content-address payload and store it through the handle's byte store.\n   476\t\n   477\t   Supports [handle payload] (defaulting to default-hash-algorithm, :blake3)\n   478\t   and [handle payload {:keys [algorithm]}].\n   479\t\n   480\t   The payload is encoded exactly once. The address is derived solely from\n   481\t   those canonical bytes, and the same bytes go to the backend effect\n   482\t   :put-bytes-fn as (put-bytes-fn address bytes). The backend must answer\n   483\t   with one of:\n   484\t\n   485\t     :inserted -- the bytes are durably stored now;\n   486\t     :present  -- bytes are already stored under that address.\n   487\t\n   488\t   Any other answer is an invalid backend result and throws: DaoJing does\n   489\t   not accept ambiguous truthiness. The address is returned only after the\n   490\t   backend reports success.\n   491\t\n   492\t   On :present the stored bytes are read back through :get-bytes-fn and\n   493\t   verified both by hash against the address and byte for byte against the\n   494\t   proposed bytes. Equal content is idempotent and return