{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_19","type":"agent_message","text":"The implementation keeps the intended separation: Jing owns canonical bytes and addressing; memory and file keep copied byte snapshots; remote and DHT validate untrusted receipts; ordinary accepted-snapshot reads do not repeat canonical re-encoding. I found no new architectural blocker. The remaining questions are documentation authority and the explicitly recorded Dart producer limitation, which I’m classifying separately from this merge’s behavior."}}
